{"text": "DARCY J. DAVIS, CPA\n10248 Allamanda Circle\nPalm Beach Gardens, FL 33410\n561.328.8915 (Residence)\n912.658.1033 (cell phone)\n\nssicpa@yahoo.com (E-mail)\n\nPROFESSIONAL EXPERIENCE\n\nHealth Care District of Palm Beach County 7/11-Present\nWest Palm Beach, FL\nThe District is a unique and complex organization, unduplicated in its current form across the country, which\nincludes a 70-bed rural hospital, with a primary care residency program, a 120 bed skilled nursing home and\nrehabilitation facility, an Aeromedical program encompassing 2 Trauma Hawk helicopters, the Trauma Agency\nfor Palm Beach County, 8 Primary Care (adults, pediatrics and dental services) FQHC\u2019s, a Medicaid HMO,\nSchool Health for over 200 county schools, an Institutional Pharmacy and Managed Care safety net products with\nmultiple benefit plan options, funded primarily by property taxes, that has a physician network in excess of 1,000\nprimary care and specialty doctors, partnerships with all 13 hospitals in the county, and an institutional pharmacy\nwith a combined annual budget of direct medical services expense in excess of $60M per year. Effectively, the\nDistrict is a mature, taxpayer-funded healthcare safety net serving as both a Health Plan and a direct patient care\nprovider, across a broad continuum of care.\n\nChief Operating Officer (7/15 \u2014 Present)\n\nResponsibilities: As a direct report to the District Board, have oversight and responsibility for all\noperational and financial functions of the $260M Special Taxing District, through direct supervision of\nthe senior management operational and financial teams.\ne Transitioning the managed care products during the implementation of the Affordable Care Act to\nrespond to community needs, while adjusting the District approach to care to a gate-keeper model,\nwhich will ultimately save the taxpayers millions through a reduction in millage.\ne Working on hospital affiliation possibilities that would provide expert resources and additional\nclinical solutions.\ne Identifying and implementing numerous opportunities to streamline and share resources across\nexisting District programs.\n\nChief Operations Officer/Chief Financial Officer (10/13 \u2014 7/15,\nResponsibilities: As a direct report to the CEO, had continued operational responsibility over the provider\nprograms, along with the financial responsibility for the entire District organization by serving as its top\nfinancial executive position.\ne Redesigned all financial and budget departments and reports to provide more transparency and\nunderstanding to interested stakeholders, as well as improved financial returns from the revenue\ncycle.\ne Key leader involved in the financial turnaround of $26M in one year from a loss position to a\npositive margin by redesigning plan benefits and improvements in provider program bottom lines.\ne Reviewed and updated all financial policies, resulting in streamlined processes and clarity around\ninvestments, equity transfers, budget transfers and general procurements.",
